#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551457} :activity/id #uuid "50cb0aa0-643b-56c3-935c-3bd9615919f8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551366 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a190c4a-9cc2-50ab-a107-16fc3f92fc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415545} {:answer/id #uuid "1e594ce1-22ea-5fd6-afb9-6b06b4b9255c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415546} {:answer/id #uuid "70323d57-c32e-523a-902e-eb0de24ca0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415554} {:answer/id #uuid "83f12e6b-62c0-5595-a194-e0065cfb501d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415557} {:answer/id #uuid "c6eb0c7d-ecb7-57ee-81fb-a558588e214e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2},\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415564} :answer-field/id #uuid "646b1b63-2cd4-5c4d-b0e4-160d844e1954" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d417d43-c45e-500b-a5bf-a441848f66ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-95378" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$  \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =2,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0f51217a-fd5d-5fe6-b533-50d56f781766" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551400}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551382 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f16480c-d86a-5db9-b802-4ced71c8377c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5},\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415549} {:answer/id #uuid "5febb191-7c5d-5f4e-82d6-efc23b4d4485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16,\\,9,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415551} {:answer/id #uuid "73c9cf54-1f9b-52f1-b8ed-dd9e193c12b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415555} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3fcfba-14a5-5b55-ba3e-4a632953d6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415560} {:answer/id #uuid "be6dbb3a-d9f4-5182-87d2-f89ac41af4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5,\\,3,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415560} :answer-field/id #uuid "b838eb18-ab2d-5fe6-b6c3-92ea8e153a8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ba2e577-1f2d-586f-a5db-7d03c7c71c22" :question/math-academy-id "q-95375" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-4\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )[(5-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4)]-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +16)-16(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "32d51e09-dfa1-5fdb-a2f2-601b26efdfc6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551366}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551394 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415548} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415558} {:answer/id #uuid "c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415563} {:answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565} :answer-field/id #uuid "2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95374" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "42d7236d-92fe-52f5-8b19-b1b09a4e3d89" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551382}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551400 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f72538-1df2-5400-9f78-cb8409f95ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367542} {:answer/id #uuid "aaed5f82-08d1-5931-9dc0-ef6782cb00fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367543} {:answer/id #uuid "85459f08-ebd2-5de2-af01-144d2aeb100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367544} {:answer/id #uuid "d4be0251-97f5-5981-bda6-e62b677f0ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367545} {:answer/id #uuid "c7dc7fb6-4c25-5dc1-b337-7a9abd5eaf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367544} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b11b93b-5ed4-5c27-8e1f-ae8a252505fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a7d5c241-f1dd-539c-bc82-e319298f04d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-139500" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}13-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 13-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (13-\\lambda )(13-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ 169-26\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-26\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "52507521-8d80-5625-b78a-9c6bf63ea91d"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551457 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0d752a-b826-5c64-be10-12da661ba4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368915} {:answer/id #uuid "013ec41c-cc86-5fe4-b29a-accf164dceb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$13$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368916} {:answer/id #uuid "24eac0e8-069f-5b0b-9420-f802df54dfb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{13}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368917} {:answer/id #uuid "a9aa8865-fb8b-5614-b9f2-9c3837814ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368918} {:answer/id #uuid "7be86b9d-e96c-5fac-9a1f-8fb3684e2c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368919}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368917} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd34787a-f30f-575c-9f6f-407c026f6c03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "40523132-fd0a-5a78-90b5-ce48c89eb124" :question/math-academy-id "q-95317" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}9-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -4\\lambda +36-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -13) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =13,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{13} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e1d62f93-fbf5-5e4e-9d59-00beb82dc703" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551394}}] :activity/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550346}]}
